WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.080
Steve: Hello everyone,
This is Steve.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.450
Steve: Today, I am speaking in Japanese.
And We have a special guest.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.520
Steve: Mr,Kazu from Kazu languages 

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.200
Kazu: Hi everyone,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.860
Steve: Hello,
So if you like my videos 

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.950
Steve: Please subscribe my channel.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:23.140
Steve: Today, I would like to
Have an interview with Kazu.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.780
Steve: Because he is able to 
speak various languages.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.690
Steve: I lived in Japan for 9 years.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.220
Steve: When I went to book stores,
I saw only English text book.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.730
Steve: Learning other languages
 it was always only English, 

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:44.220
Steve: And little bit of Chinese,
Spanish, Korean, That was how it was.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.910
Steve: Then, It was told that 

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:51.330
Steve: Japanese people don’t care 
about other languages except English.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.740
Steve: But Mr,Kazu
Could you please introduce 

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:00.800
Steve: about your channel and

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.510
Steve: explain which languages 
You’ve studied.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:08.000
Steve: To my audience.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.780
Kazu: My main reason for studying 
other languages is

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:19.230
Kazu: to communicate with
other people and make friends.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:26.150
Kazu: Learning new languages will
empower me to learn more about other cultures.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:32.260
Kazu: To see how people react to
What you speak.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.030
Kazu: And by leaning those languages 

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:38.560
Kazu: I believe there’s a connection 
between leaning and respecting their cultures.

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:44.450
Kazu: In my channel,
I am having conversations with

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.900
Kazu: various people from different countries 
in their mother language.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:55.520
Kazu: Now, I am able to speak Japanese,
English, Spanish, French, Portuguese,

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.400
Kazu: Indonesian, Russian, Arabic,
Those are the languages I am studying now.

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:04.930
Steve: Interesting thing is

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:12.160
Steve: Romance languages,
For example French, Italian, Portuguese,

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.760
Steve: These are easy.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:21.760
Kazu: But in your case,
Slavic languages like Indonesian, Arabic,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:29.510
Steve: and Languages in Europe,
Your interest is wide range.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:35.520
Steve: How do you choose to study 
those languages?

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:40.140
Kazu: There’s very important point

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.780
Kazu: when I decide to study new languages 

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.490
That is I want to study 
Languages that’s completely opposite 

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.410
Kazu: to my lifestyle.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:53.170
Kazu: For example, 
Difference of cultures from my standpoint.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:58.310
Kazu: or difference of lifestyles,
I want to study languages

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.700
Kazu: That has different cultures from Japan 

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:06.280
Kazu: So I am intentionally choosing 
languages that is other group of language family.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.670
Kazu: I am choosing widely 

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.920
Kazu: so I’ll have opportunity to
learn about many other countries. 

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.210
Steve: When you visit Europe.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:21.980
Steve: There’s some like..

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:27.300
Steve: People gather at pub

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:35.540
Steve: And put national flags 
on their chest that they are able to speak 

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.580
Steve: and have conversations with 
various languages 

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:41.000
Steve: sometimes swap their seats,
There’s things like that.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:45.840
Steve: Of course, There’s other languages 
right next to your country in Europe.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.520
Steve: So there are many people 
Who is able to speak other languages.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:51.980
Steve: How about Japan?

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:54.480
Steve: Is there any movement of people 

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.480
Steve: like wanting to study 
various languages?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.320
Steve: Is there anything like that?

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:06.980
Kazu: Well.. There are not much
in Japan yet, But

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.510
Kazu: People’s attention to 
English has been increased 

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:15.640
Kazu: Long time ago, Japanese was told that
We are the nation not good at speaking other languages 

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.470
Kazu: But things changed 

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.400
Kazu: There are many people 
Whom taking English class seriously 

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.970
Kazu: Another example is, 
Some people choose to study 

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:30.080
Kazu: Spanish, Chinese and other languages 

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.560
Kazu: as second language at the college.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:38.500
Kazu: I sense that people are 
starting to change

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.830
Kazu: Their attitude toward Languages.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:46.070
Steve: English or Spanish, Russian..

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:49.610
Steve: There’s this thing called 
comprehensible input.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.570
Steve: There are many
interesting contents 

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:53.950
Steve: like podcast,

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.690
Steve: or TV channels,
There are many of them.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.180
Steve: In my case, 
I am having difficult time with Arabic.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.620
Steve: I am struggling.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:09.220
Steve: To find right audio and text books 

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.200
Steve: for my level.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.500
Steve: It’s difficult to find them.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:17.390
Steve: So, I have no idea 
about Indonesian.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:21.220
Steve: How do you find 
materials to study

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.520
Steve: Indonesian and Arabic 

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:28.030
Steve: That matches to your level and

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:33.030
Steve: gives you interest into it?

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.540
Steve: Are you having difficult time?
Kazu: Well, Yes, It’s very difficult 

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.160
Kazu: Especially finding 
Egyptian dialect in Arabic.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.280
Kazu: There’s no such a thing on the internet.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.160
Kazu: So…

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:50.460
Kazu: Mainly I watch 
YouTube and Netflix.

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:58.380
Steve: Certainly, 
YouTube is the best source.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:01.980
Kazu: Yes, I agree with you.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:06.050
Steve: There are many Lebanese as well.
Kazu: Ah Lebanese, Yes.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.360
Steve: I get confused between 
Lebanese and Arabic.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:12.850
Steve: Sometimes I listen to
Lebanese and Egyptian.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:18.340
Steve: And listen to standard Arabic,
These are very difficult.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:20.580
Kazu: There are so many various languages.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.140
Steve: Yes.

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:25.330
Steve: So, Do you live in Japan?

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:28.770
Kazu: Yes, I live in Japan 
for most of my life.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:34.510
Steve: Are you planning to 
visit abroad ?

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:38.860
Kazu: Well, For now I want to focus on
studying languages.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.500
Kazu: But maybe next year or
the year after next

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:45.520
Kazu: I want to visit countries 
where main languages are

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:48.860
Kazu: What I  learned.
Steve: That makes scene.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:55.650
Steve: The thing about trip like that

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:59.840
Steve: When you visit those countries 

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:01.860
Steve: After you study hard

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:05.610
Steve: It’s like a dream… like a dream.
Kazu: Certainly, It is special.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.230
Steve: Being able to use

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:11.100
Steve: languages that you studied hard

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:15.070
Steve: In your daily life

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:19.140
Steve: Is such a special thing.
Kazu: Yes.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:24.380
Steve: Is there any particular countries,
Like South America or Europe or Russia

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:28.350
Steve: Or Egypt,
Closest to Indonesia.

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:29.060
Kazu: Well 

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:33.510
Kazu: First, Since I have lot of friends 
in Indonesia, So I want to visit there.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:37.930
Kazu: And I studied both 
Portuguese and Spanish 

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:43.940
Kazu: so I want to visit South America as well,
I just want to see whole world.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.190
Steve: Very well then.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.730
Steve: I think 

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:52.220
Steve: Anybody should be able to 
learn multiple languages 

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:56.350
Steve: Not only one language,

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:59.890
Steve: And there’s such a great 
technologies like MP3 and others,

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:06.240
Steve: So we are able to study 
much easier than how it used to be.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:12.600
Steve: And your life will get richer.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:20.100
Steve: So I could say that
 you are a discoverer 

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:24.940
Steve: of languages.
Kazu: Discoverer.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.540
Kazu: I am humbled.
Steve: OK, so.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:33.500
Steve: I will leave link
of your YouTube channel 

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.490
Steve: Into description box.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:10:01.760
[Speaking Spanish］

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:04.260
Steve: So far, What I could understand is

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:07.930
Steve: Only Bahasa Indonesia!

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:13.180
Steve: I’ll study Indonesian 
in the future.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:16.470
Steve: OK! Thank you.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:17.740
Steve: That was fun.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.520
Steve: I wish you all the best.
Kazu: Thank you.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.280
Steve: Please study
 10 and 20 more languages 

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:25.870
Steve: Since you are so much younger than me.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:30.000
Kazu: Yes, I will do my best. Thank you so much.
